From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 07:23:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] svga: allow R8G8B8A8_UNORM display targets

The display-target override in svga_is_format_supported() and
svga_is_dx_format_supported() accepts R8G8B8A8_UNORM_SRGB but not
R8G8B8A8_UNORM. The DRI frontend therefore creates RGBA-ordered
configs only as sRGB-capable ones.

On Android this leaves no usable window config. droid_add_configs_for_visuals()
builds the HAL_PIXEL_FORMAT_RGBA_8888 configs from those sRGB DRI configs
alone, so dri_config[1][0] (double-buffered, linear) stays NULL. It then
skips BGRA_8888 because RGBA configs exist. hwui creates its window surfaces
with EGL_GL_COLORSPACE_LINEAR_KHR, so every eglCreateWindowSurface() fails:

  EGL user error 0x3009 (EGL_BAD_MATCH) in eglCreateWindowSurface:
      Unsupported surfacetype/colorspace configuration

and every app aborts on its first frame with "drawRenderNode called on a
context with no surface!". Seen with Waydroid (Android 11, Mesa 23.2.1)
on VirtualBox VMSVGA with a VGPU10 device.

Accept R8G8B8A8_UNORM as a display target too, next to its sRGB variant.
The host capability query that follows still decides whether the format
is usable.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/gallium/drivers/svga/svga_format.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/svga/svga_format.c b/src/gallium/drivers/svga/svga_format.c
index 7228a8c..80888bb 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/svga/svga_format.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/svga/svga_format.c
@@ -2251,6 +2251,7 @@ svga_is_format_supported(struct pipe_screen *screen,
       case SVGA3D_B5G6R5_UNORM:
       case SVGA3D_B8G8R8X8_UNORM_SRGB:
       case SVGA3D_B8G8R8A8_UNORM_SRGB:
+      case SVGA3D_R8G8B8A8_UNORM:
       case SVGA3D_R8G8B8A8_UNORM_SRGB:
          break;
 
@@ -2377,6 +2378,7 @@ svga_is_dx_format_supported(struct pipe_screen *screen,
       case SVGA3D_B5G6R5_UNORM:
       case SVGA3D_B8G8R8X8_UNORM_SRGB:
       case SVGA3D_B8G8R8A8_UNORM_SRGB:
+      case SVGA3D_R8G8B8A8_UNORM:
       case SVGA3D_R8G8B8A8_UNORM_SRGB:
          break;
 
